From ac93d4538f6d069922e21fe59cc715ae32851384 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunrisepeak <speakshen@163.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 19:02:06 +0900
Subject: [clangd] Module compile commands follow their real inputs

Compilation database generations are reloaded when response-file inputs change, external module commands resolve from the requesting project, the optional overlay command mangler is guarded during module scans, and command adjustment preserves the GCC module-mapper dialect. Fixture paths are serialized as JSON so the tests hold on Windows.

* clangd: reload immutable CDB generations when response inputs change

  Retain response bytes per generation, detect nested and failed inputs, and refresh provider inventories on exact input changes. Validate coherent publication and preserve old generation commands. Include actual disk same-size/full-mtime provider association regression.

* [clangd] Serialize response generation fixture paths as JSON

* [clangd] Resolve external module commands from the requesting project

* [clangd] Guard the optional overlay command mangler during module scans

* clangd: preserve GCC module mapper dialect in command adjustment
